<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41255" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτάρροθος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίρροθος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>helper, defender,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of the gods that help in fight, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.366
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.182
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχης ἐ.</span>
			<i>in</i> fight, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.339
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαναοῖσι μάχης ἐπιτάρροθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.180
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμμα δίκης ἐπιτάρροθον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Maiist.
					59
				</span></i>
			 : as fem., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοίη οἱ ἐγὼν ἐπιτάρροθος ἦα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.808
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				828
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίκα..καλῶν ἐ. ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Terp.
					6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>master, lord,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεγέης</span> Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.67
			</span></i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάρροθος.</span></div>
